LANTERN — ZB04 SHROUD CRAWLER
One-direction creative animation test, 7 October 2026.

WHAT TO WATCH
previews/shroud_crawler_motion_comparison_60hz.mp4 shows both actions side by side at native drawing scale.
Cocoon scoot: six drawings, 44 ticks / 0.733333 seconds, looping. An asymmetric hand-pull/surge, shroud contraction, and a soft body-flop rather than a human walk. The drawings do not establish a mechanically alternating arm gait.
Predatory pounce: six drawings, 50 ticks / 0.833333 seconds, one-shot. Readable gather/coiled lift, a 3-tick launch, impact, recovery. The preview holds recovery18 extra ticks between repetitions; those18 ticks are not in the runtime clip.
Half-speed videos retain60Hz output and double drawing exposures.
60Hz describes playback timing. There are SIX unique drawings per action, not60 unique drawings per second. No tweening or generated in-between pixels.

