COMMON REGISTRATION
Both clips use the same768×768 canvas and root at(448,488) pixels measured from the top-left. Normalized bottom-left pivot is(0.5833333333,0.3645833333).
Original sheet cell origins remain fixed512×512 apart. Each figure is translated exactly+128,+128 from its source cell coordinates, without per-frame centering, scale fitting, warping, rotation, or mirroring.
Native reaches beyond nominal sheet gutters are preserved with connected-figure ownership. Large common margins protect every fingertip and cloth edge. Intentional pounce displacement and cloth-volume changes remain intact.
Root/pivot is a proposed consistent import coordinate, not a calibrated physical root. In-engine movement speed, attack distance, collider, pixels-per-unit, and all other directions remain future tuning decisions. Do not automatically resize individual sprites to their bounds.

ART DIRECTION AND LIMITS
Screen down-right, world+X. Orthographic35.2643897° elevation /45° azimuth is the prompt target. Elevated gameplay silhouettes were visually reviewed; a generative raster sheet is not mathematical camera certification.
Two visible connected human arms/hands; lower body fully enclosed in one charcoal/ivory shroud; no exposed legs or stumps. Cocoon squashing/coiling is deliberate. This is an expressive stepped-animation experiment for style/motion review, not an approved finished enemy rig.
Individual fingers are simplified/overlapped in some planted-hand drawings. Minor cloth-fold and head-angle variation remains between drawings. No further polishing or human walking was substituted for the creature motion.

PROVENANCE
Built-in imagegen; fresh drawings from the original character identity/style reference only. Prompts include the requested words Sunburst2.5 (spaced as Sunburst 2.5 in the actual generation prompts). The tool does not expose proof of backend model selection.
First locomotion4×2 attempt was rejected for edge clipping. One fresh3×2 retry succeeded; the original attempt is retained only in the source archive. Attack succeeded on its first fresh sheet. No generative edit cascade.
Only deterministic extraction, uniform transparent padding, alpha-only cleanup, atlas assembly and preview compositing were applied. Source RGBA sheets are preserved byte-for-byte. Surviving runtime RGB values equal native source RGB exactly. Alpha≤16 becomes0; alpha≥250 becomes255. Tiny detached background specks are removed by component ownership. Hidden transparent RGB haze in the raw viewer does not appear in real alpha composites.

